From 8959dbf638797d75d5250844991efea8199416ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:16:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: an embedder can share a linked stylesheet's parsed
 contents

A document parses every stylesheet it links, even when the embedder
delivers the same bytes to many documents. `DocumentConfig` now takes
`SharedStylesheets`: when a linked sheet's bytes arrive, the document
asks it for the sheet's parsed contents, and wraps them in a stylesheet
of its own (its own lock, its own `media`) instead of parsing.

`parse_shared_stylesheet` parses contents any document can read: on a
read-only lock, as Stylo's user agent sheets are, with `@import`s
resolved while it parses. An import it cannot resolve then makes the
sheet unshareable, since a pending import is written in later through
the sheet's lock. A shared sheet's imports have their `@font-face`
fonts fetched by the document, as its own imports do.
---
